    "body": "Optional feedback: it took me a while to realize the interacting roles of _i_, _potentialSuffixIndeX_, and _inputIndex_. I might do something like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\n1. Let i be 1.\r\n2. While true:\r\n  1. Let potentialSuffixIndex = potentialSuffix.length - i.\r\n  2. Let inputIndex = input.length - i.\r\n  3. If potentialSuffixIndex < 0, then return true.\r\n  4. If inputIndex < 0, then return false.\r\n  5. Let potentialSuffixCodeUnit = potentialSuffix[potentialSuffixIndex].\r\n  6. Let inputCodeUnit = input[inputIndex].\r\n  7. Return false if potentialSuffixCodeUnit != inputCodeUnit.\r\n  8. Set i to i + 1.\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever I can easily see how what you have here is closer to \"code unit prefix\", and so then you could get carried away trying to make them both use something like the above... so, very optional feedback.",
